(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[2] = [{"v":1,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":"सञ्जय उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"तं तथा कृपयाऽविष्टमश्रुपूर्णाकुलेक्षणम् ।\nविषीदन्तमिदं वाक्यमुवाच मधुसूदनः ॥","iast":"taṃ tathā kṛpayā’viṣṭamaśrupūrṇākulekṣaṇam |\nviṣīdantamidaṃ vākyamuvāca madhusūdanaḥ ||","read":"tam tathaa kripayaa'vishtamashrupoornaakulekshanam |\nvisheedantamidam vaakyamuvaacha madhusoodanah ||","spli":"sañjaya uvāca","splr":"sanjaya uvaacha","en":"Sanjaya said: To him thus with pity overcome, with smarting brimming eyes, despondent, Madhusûdana spake these words:","en2":"To him who was thus overwhelmed with pity and sorrowing, and whose eyes were dimmed with tears, Madhusudana spoke these words:","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Sanjaya tells the king that Arjuna was overcome with pity and sorrow, his eyes full of tears. Then Krishna spoke these words to him."},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"कुतस्त्वा कश्मलमिदं विषमे समुपस्थितम् ।\nअनार्यजुष्टमस्वर्ग्यमकीर्तिकरमर्जुन ॥","iast":"kutastvā kaśmalamidaṃ viṣame samupasthitam |\nanāryajuṣṭamasvargyamakīrtikaramarjuna ||","read":"kutastvaa kashmalamidam vishame samupasthitam |\nanaaryajushtamasvargyamakeertikaramarjuna ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Whence hath this dejection befallen thee in this perilous strait, ignoble, heaven-closing, infamous, O Arjuna?","en2":"In such a crisis, whence comes upon thee, O Arjuna, this dejection, un-Aryalike, disgraceful and contrary to the attainment of heaven?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna asks Arjuna where this sadness has come from at such a hard moment. He says it is not noble, it brings shame, and it closes the way to heaven."},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"क्लैब्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ नैतत्त्वय्युपपद्यते ।\nक्षुद्रं हृदयदौर्बल्यं त्यक्त्वोत्तिष्ठ परन्तप ॥","iast":"klaibyaṃ mā sma gamaḥ pārtha naitattvayyupapadyate |\nkṣudraṃ hṛdayadaurbalyaṃ tyaktvottiṣṭha parantapa ||","read":"klaibyam maa sma gamah paartha naitattvayyupapadyate |\nkshudram hridayadaurbalyam tyaktvottishtha parantapa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yield not to impotence, O Partha! it doth not befit thee. Shake off this paltry faint-heartedness! Stand up, Parantapa!","en2":"Yield not to unmanliness, O son of Prithâ! Ill doth it become thee. Cast off this mean faint-heartedness and arise, O scorcher of thine enemies!","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna not to give in to this weakness, because it does not suit him. He should throw off this mean loss of courage and stand up."},{"v":4,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"कथं भीष्ममहं संख्ये द्रोणं च मधुसूदन ।\nइषुभिः प्रतियोत्स्यामि पूजार्हावरिसूदन ॥","iast":"kathaṃ bhīṣmamahaṃ saṃkhye droṇaṃ ca madhusūdana |\niṣubhiḥ pratiyotsyāmi pūjārhāvarisūdana ||","read":"katham bheeshmamaham samkhye dronam cha madhusoodana |\nishubhih pratiyotsyaami poojaarhaavarisoodana ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: How, O Madhusûdana, shall I attack Bhîshma and Drona with arrows in battle, they who are worthy of reverence, O slayer of foes?","en2":"—But how can I, in battle, O slayer of Madhu, fight with arrows against Bhishma and Drona, who are rather worthy to be worshipped, O destroyer of foes!","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna how he can shoot arrows in battle at Bhishma and Drona. They are people who deserve his deepest respect."},{"v":5,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"गुरूनहत्वा हि महानुभावान् ।\nश्रेयो भोक्तुं भैक्ष्यमपीह लोके ।\nहत्वार्थकामांस्तु गुरूनिहैव ।\nभुञ्जीय भोगान् रुधिरप्रदिग्धान् ॥","iast":"gurūnahatvā hi mahānubhāvān |\nśreyo bhoktuṃ bhaikṣyamapīha loke |\nhatvārthakāmāṃstu gurūnihaiva |\nbhuñjīya bhogān rudhirapradigdhān ||","read":"guroonahatvaa hi mahaanubhaavaan |\nshreyo bhoktum bhaikshyamapeeha loke |\nhatvaarthakaamaamstu guroonihaiva |\nbhunjeeya bhogaan rudhirapradigdhaan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Better in this world to eat even the beggar's crust than to slay these most noble Gurus. Slaying these Gurus, our well-wishers, I should taste of blood-besprinkled feasts.","en2":"Surely it would be better even to eat the bread of beggary in this life than to slay these great-souled masters. But if I kill them, even in this world, all my enjoyment of wealth and desires will be stained with blood.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna says it would be better to live as a beggar than to kill his great teachers. If he killed them, every pleasure he had would be stained with blood."},{"v":6,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न चैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो ।\nयद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः ।\nयानेव हत्वा न जिजीविषाम ।\nस्तेऽवस्थिताः प्रमुखे धार्तराष्ट्राः ॥","iast":"na caitadvidmaḥ kataranno garīyo |\nyadvā jayema yadi vā no jayeyuḥ |\nyāneva hatvā na jijīviṣāma |\nste’vasthitāḥ pramukhe dhārtarāṣṭrāḥ ||","read":"na chaitadvidmah kataranno gareeyo |\nyadvaa jayema yadi vaa no jayeyuh |\nyaaneva hatvaa na jijeevishaama |\nste'vasthitaah pramukhe dhaartaraashtraah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor know I which for us be the better, that we conquer them or they conquer us—these, whom having slain we should not care to live, even these arrayed against us, the sons of Dhritarâshtra.","en2":"And indeed I can scarcely tell which will be better, that we should conquer them, or that they should conquer us. The very sons of Dhritarâshtra,—after slaying whom we should not care to live,—stand facing us.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna says he does not know which is better, that they win or that the other side wins. After killing the sons of Dhritarashtra, who face them now, he would not even want to live."},{"v":7,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कार्पण्यदोषोपहतस्वभावः ।\nपृच्छामि त्वां धर्मसंमूढचेताः ।\nयच्छ्रेयः स्यान्निश्चितं ब्रूहि तन्मे ।\nशिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नम् ॥","iast":"kārpaṇyadoṣopahatasvabhāvaḥ |\npṛcchāmi tvāṃ dharmasaṃmūḍhacetāḥ |\nyacchreyaḥ syānniścitaṃ brūhi tanme |\nśiṣyaste’haṃ śādhi māṃ tvāṃ prapannam ||","read":"kaarpanyadoshopahatasvabhaavah |\nprichchhaami tvaam dharmasammoodhachetaah |\nyachchhreyah syaannishchitam broohi tanme |\nshishyaste'ham shaadhi maam tvaam prapannam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"My heart is weighed down with the vice of faintness; my mind is confused as to duty. I ask thee which may be the better—that tell me decisively. I am thy disciple, suppliant to Thee; teach me.","en2":"With my nature overpowered by weak commiseration, with a mind in confusion about duty, I supplicate Thee. Say decidedly what is good for me. I am Thy disciple. Instruct me who have taken refuge in Thee.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna tells Krishna that his heart is weak and his mind is confused about his duty. He asks Krishna to tell him clearly what is best. He offers himself as a student and asks to be taught."},{"v":8,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न हि प्रपश्यामि ममापनुद्याद् ।\nयच्छोकमुच्छोषणमिन्द्रियाणाम् ।\nअवाप्य भूमावसपत्नमृद्धं ।\nराज्यं सुराणामपि चाधिपत्यम् ॥","iast":"na hi prapaśyāmi mamāpanudyād |\nyacchokamucchoṣaṇamindriyāṇām |\navāpya bhūmāvasapatnamṛddhaṃ |\nrājyaṃ surāṇāmapi cādhipatyam ||","read":"na hi prapashyaami mamaapanudyaad |\nyachchhokamuchchhoshanamindriyaanaam |\navaapya bhoomaavasapatnamriddham |\nraajyam suraanaamapi chaadhipatyam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For I see not that it would drive away this anguish that withers up my senses, if I should attain unrivalled monarchy on earth, or even the sovereignty of the Shining Ones.","en2":"I do not see anything to remove this sorrow which blasts my senses, even were I to obtain unrivalled and flourishing dominion over the earth, and mastery over the gods.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna says nothing can take away the sorrow that is drying up his senses. Not even ruling the whole earth without a rival, or ruling over the gods."},{"v":9,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":"सञ्जय उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"एवमुक्त्वा हृषीकेशं गुडाकेशः परन्तप ।\nन योत्स्य इति गोविन्दमुक्त्वा तूष्णीं बभूव ह ॥","iast":"evamuktvā hṛṣīkeśaṃ guḍākeśaḥ parantapa |\nna yotsya iti govindamuktvā tūṣṇīṃ babhūva ha ||","read":"evamuktvaa hrisheekesham gudaakeshah parantapa |\nna yotsya iti govindamuktvaa tooshneem babhoova ha ||","spli":"sañjaya uvāca","splr":"sanjaya uvaacha","en":"Sanjaya said: Gudâkesha, conqueror of his foes, having thus addressed Hrishîkesha and said to Govinda, \"I will not fight!\", became silent.","en2":"Having spoken thus to the Lord of the senses, Gudâkesha, the scorcher of foes, said to Govinda, \"I shall not fight,\" and became silent.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Sanjaya tells the king that Arjuna, the conqueror of his enemies, said to Krishna, 'I will not fight!' and then fell silent."},{"v":10,"sp":"sanjaya","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तमुवाच हृषीकेशः प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये विषीदन्तमिदं वचः ॥","iast":"tamuvāca hṛṣīkeśaḥ prahasanniva bhārata |\nsenayorubhayormadhye viṣīdantamidaṃ vacaḥ ||","read":"tamuvaacha hrisheekeshah prahasanniva bhaarata |\nsenayorubhayormadhye visheedantamidam vachah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Then Hrishîkesha, smiling, as it were, O Bhârata, spake these words to him, despondent, in the midst of the two armies:","en2":"To him who was sorrowing in the midst of the two armies, Hrishikesha, as if smiling, O descendant of Bharata! spoke these words.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Sanjaya tells the king that Krishna, as if smiling, spoke to the sorrowing Arjuna there, in the middle of the two armies."},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"अशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे ।\nगतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः ॥","iast":"aśocyānanvaśocastvaṃ prajñāvādāṃśca bhāṣase |\ngatāsūnagatāsūṃśca nānuśocanti paṇḍitāḥ ||","read":"ashochyaananvashochastvam prajnaavaadaamshcha bhaashase |\ngataasoonagataasoomshcha naanushochanti panditaah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Thou grievest for those that should not be griev ed for, yet speakest words of wisdom. The wise grieve neither for the living nor for the dead.","en2":"Thou hast been mourning for them who should not be mourned for. Yet thou speakest words of wisdom. The (truly) wise grieve neither for the living nor the dead.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he is sad for those who need no sadness, even while he speaks wise words. The truly wise grieve neither for the living nor for the dead."},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न त्वेवाहं जातु नासं न त्वं नेमे जनाधिपाः ।\nन चैव न भविष्यामः सर्वे वयमतः परम् ॥","iast":"na tvevāhaṃ jātu nāsaṃ na tvaṃ neme janādhipāḥ |\nna caiva na bhaviṣyāmaḥ sarve vayamataḥ param ||","read":"na tvevaaham jaatu naasam na tvam neme janaadhipaah |\nna chaiva na bhavishyaamah sarve vayamatah param ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor at any time verily was I not, nor thou, nor these princes of men, nor verily shall we ever cease to be, hereafter.","en2":"It is not that I have never existed, nor thou, nor these kings. Nor is it that we shall cease to exist in the future.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says there was never a time when he did not exist, nor Arjuna, nor these kings. And none of them will ever stop existing in the future."},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"देहिनोऽस्मिन्यथा देहे कौमारं यौवनं जरा ।\nतथा देहान्तरप्राप्तिर्धीरस्तत्र न मुह्यति ॥","iast":"dehino’sminyathā dehe kaumāraṃ yauvanaṃ jarā |\ntathā dehāntaraprāptirdhīrastatra na muhyati ||","read":"dehino'sminyathaa dehe kaumaaram yauvanam jaraa |\ntathaa dehaantarapraaptirdheerastatra na muhyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As the dweller in the body experienceth in the body childhood, youth, old age, so passeth he on to another body; the steadfast one grieveth not thereat.","en2":"As are childhood, youth, and old age, in this body, to the embodied soul, so also is the attaining of another body. Calm souls are not deluded thereat.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the one who lives in the body passes through childhood, youth and old age. In the same way, it passes on to another body. Calm, steady people are not troubled by this."},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मात्रास्पर्शास्तु कौन्तेय शीतोष्णसुखदुःखदाः ।\nआगमापायिनोऽनित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत ॥","iast":"mātrāsparśāstu kaunteya śītoṣṇasukhaduḥkhadāḥ |\nāgamāpāyino’nityāstāṃstitikṣasva bhārata ||","read":"maatraasparshaastu kaunteya sheetoshnasukhaduhkhadaah |\naagamaapaayino'nityaastaamstitikshasva bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The contacts of matter, O son of Kuntî, giving cold and heat, pleasure and pain, they come and go, impermanent; endure them bravely, O Bhârata.","en2":"Notions of heat and cold, of pain and pleasure, are born, O son of Kunti, only of the contact of the senses with their objects. They have a beginning and an end. They are impermanent in their nature. Bear them patiently, O descendant of Bharata.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that cold and heat, pleasure and pain, come when the senses touch things. They come and go and do not last. He should bear them bravely."},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यं हि न व्यथयन्त्येते पुरुषं पुरुषर्षभ ।\nसमदुःखसुखं धीरं सोऽमृतत्वाय कल्पते ॥","iast":"yaṃ hi na vyathayantyete puruṣaṃ puruṣarṣabha |\nsamaduḥkhasukhaṃ dhīraṃ so’mṛtatvāya kalpate ||","read":"yam hi na vyathayantyete purusham purusharshabha |\nsamaduhkhasukham dheeram so'mritatvaaya kalpate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The man whom these torment not, O chief of men, balanced in pain and pleasure, steadfast, he is fitted for immortality.","en2":"That calm man who is the same in pain and pleasure, whom these cannot disturb, alone is able, O great amongst men, to attain to immortality.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a calm person who stays the same in pain and pleasure, and is not troubled by them, is able to reach immortality."},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नासतो विद्यते भावो नाभावो विद्यते सतः ।\nउभयोरपि दृष्टोऽन्तस्त्वनयोस्तत्त्वदर्शिभिः ॥","iast":"nāsato vidyate bhāvo nābhāvo vidyate sataḥ |\nubhayorapi dṛṣṭo’ntastvanayostattvadarśibhiḥ ||","read":"naasato vidyate bhaavo naabhaavo vidyate satah |\nubhayorapi drishto'ntastvanayostattvadarshibhih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The unreal hath no being; the real never ceaseth to be; the truth about both hath been perceived by the seers of the essence of things.","en2":"The unreal never is. The Real never is not. Men possessed of the knowledge of the Truth fully know both these.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says what is unreal never exists, and what is real never stops existing. Those who know the truth have seen this about both."},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अविनाशि तु तद्विद्धि येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ।\nविनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित् कर्तुमर्हति ॥","iast":"avināśi tu tadviddhi yena sarvamidaṃ tatam |\nvināśamavyayasyāsya na kaścit kartumarhati ||","read":"avinaashi tu tadviddhi yena sarvamidam tatam |\nvinaashamavyayasyaasya na kashchit kartumarhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Know That to be indestructible by whom all this is pervaded. Nor can any work the destruction of that imperishable One.","en2":"That by which all this is pervaded,—That know for certain to be indestructible. None has the power to destroy this Immutable.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to know that the One that fills all this can never be destroyed. No one has the power to destroy it."},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अन्तवन्त इमे देहा नित्यस्योक्ताः शरीरिणः ।\nअनाशिनोऽप्रमेयस्य तस्माद्युध्यस्व भारत ॥","iast":"antavanta ime dehā nityasyoktāḥ śarīriṇaḥ |\nanāśino’prameyasya tasmādyudhyasva bhārata ||","read":"antavanta ime dehaa nityasyoktaah shareerinah |\nanaashino'prameyasya tasmaadyudhyasva bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"These bodies of the embodied One, who is eternal, indestructible and immeasurable, are known as finite. Therefore fight, O Bhârata.","en2":"Of this indwelling Self, the ever-changeless, the indestructible, the illimitable,—these bodies are said to have an end. Fight therefore, O descendant of Bharata.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the bodies come to an end, but the Self who lives in them is eternal, cannot be destroyed and cannot be measured. So he tells Arjuna to fight."},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"य एनं वेत्ति हन्तारं यश्चैनं मन्यते हतम् ।\nउभौ तौ न विजानीतो नायं हन्ति न हन्यते ॥","iast":"ya enaṃ vetti hantāraṃ yaścainaṃ manyate hatam |\nubhau tau na vijānīto nāyaṃ hanti na hanyate ||","read":"ya enam vetti hantaaram yashchainam manyate hatam |\nubhau tau na vijaaneeto naayam hanti na hanyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who regardeth this as a slayer, and he who thinketh he is slain, both of them are ignorant. He slayeth not, nor is he slain.","en2":"He who takes the Self to be the slayer, he who takes It to be the slain, neither of these knows. It does not slay, nor is It slain.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that anyone who thinks the Self kills, or thinks it is killed, does not understand. The Self does not kill, and it is not killed."},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न जायते म्रियते वा कदाचि ।\nन्नायं भूत्वा भविता वा न भूयः ।\nअजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणो ।\nन हन्यते हन्यमाने शरीरे ॥","iast":"na jāyate mriyate vā kadāci |\nnnāyaṃ bhūtvā bhavitā vā na bhūyaḥ |\najo nityaḥ śāśvato’yaṃ purāṇo |\nna hanyate hanyamāne śarīre ||","read":"na jaayate mriyate vaa kadaachi |\nnnaayam bhootvaa bhavitaa vaa na bhooyah |\najo nityah shaashvato'yam puraano |\nna hanyate hanyamaane shareere ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He is not born, nor doth he die; nor having been, ceaseth he any more to be; unborn, perpetual, eternal and ancient, he is not slain when the body is slaughtered.","en2":"This in never born, nor does It die. It is not that not having been It again comes into being. (Or according to another view: It is not that having been It again ceases to be). This is unborn, eternal, changeless, ever-Itself. It is not killed when the body is killed.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the Self is never born and never dies, and it does not stop being. It is unborn and eternal. It is not killed when the body is killed."},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वेदाविनाशिनं नित्यं य एनमजमव्ययम् ।\nकथं स पुरुषः पार्थ कं घातयति हन्ति कम् ॥","iast":"vedāvināśinaṃ nityaṃ ya enamajamavyayam |\nkathaṃ sa puruṣaḥ pārtha kaṃ ghātayati hanti kam ||","read":"vedaavinaashinam nityam ya enamajamavyayam |\nkatham sa purushah paartha kam ghaatayati hanti kam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Who knoweth him indestructible, perpetual, unborn, undiminishing, how can that man slay, O Pârtha, or cause to be slain?","en2":"He that knows This to be indestructible, changeless, without birth, and immutable, how is he, O son of Prithâ, to slay or cause another to slay?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna asks Arjuna this: if someone knows that the one who lives in the body can never be destroyed, is never born and never changes, how can that person kill, or make another kill?"},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वासांसि जीर्णानि यथा विहाय ।\nनवानि गृह्णाति नरोऽपराणि ।\nतथा शरीराणि विहाय जीर्णा ।\nन्यन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही ॥","iast":"vāsāṃsi jīrṇāni yathā vihāya |\nnavāni gṛhṇāti naro’parāṇi |\ntathā śarīrāṇi vihāya jīrṇā |\nnyanyāni saṃyāti navāni dehī ||","read":"vaasaamsi jeernaani yathaa vihaaya |\nnavaani grihnaati naro'paraani |\ntathaa shareeraani vihaaya jeernaa |\nnyanyaani samyaati navaani dehee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As a man, casting off worn-out garments, taketh new ones, so the dweller in the body, casting off worn-out bodies, entereth into others that are new.","en2":"Even as a man casts off worn-out clothes, and puts on others which are new, so the embodied casts off worn-out bodies, and enters into others which are new.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that as a person throws away worn-out clothes and puts on new ones, the one who lives in the body leaves worn-out bodies and enters new ones."},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नैनं छिन्दन्ति शस्त्राणि नैनं दहति पावकः ।\nन चैनं क्लेदयन्त्यापो न शोषयति मारुतः ॥","iast":"nainaṃ chindanti śastrāṇi nainaṃ dahati pāvakaḥ |\nna cainaṃ kledayantyāpo na śoṣayati mārutaḥ ||","read":"nainam chhindanti shastraani nainam dahati paavakah |\nna chainam kledayantyaapo na shoshayati maarutah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Weapons cleave him not, nor fire burneth him, nor waters wet him, nor wind drieth him away.","en2":"This (Self), weapons cut not; This, fire burns not; This, water wets not; and This, wind dries not.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says weapons cannot cut the Self. Fire cannot burn it, water cannot wet it, and wind cannot dry it."},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अच्छेद्योऽयमदाह्योऽयमक्लेद्योऽशोष्य एव च ।\nनित्यः सर्वगतः स्थाणुरचलोऽयं सनातनः ॥","iast":"acchedyo’yamadāhyo’yamakledyo’śoṣya eva ca |\nnityaḥ sarvagataḥ sthāṇuracalo’yaṃ sanātanaḥ ||","read":"achchhedyo'yamadaahyo'yamakledyo'shoshya eva cha |\nnityah sarvagatah sthaanurachalo'yam sanaatanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Uncleavable he, incombustible he, and indeed neither to be wetted nor dried away; perpetual, all-pervasive, stable, immovable, ancient.","en2":"This Self cannot be cut, nor burnt, nor wetted, nor dried. Changeless, all-pervading, unmoving, immovable, the Self is eternal.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the Self cannot be cut, burnt, wetted or dried. It lasts for ever, it is everywhere, it never changes and it does not move."},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अव्यक्तोऽयमचिन्त्योऽयमविकार्योऽयमुच्यते ।\nतस्मादेवं विदित्वैनं नानुशोचितुमर्हसि ॥","iast":"avyakto’yamacintyo’yamavikāryo’yamucyate |\ntasmādevaṃ viditvainaṃ nānuśocitumarhasi ||","read":"avyakto'yamachintyo'yamavikaaryo'yamuchyate |\ntasmaadevam viditvainam naanushochitumarhasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Unmanifest, unthinkable, immutable, he is called; therefore knowing him as such, thou shouldst not grieve.","en2":"This (Self) is said to be unmanifested, unthinkable, and unchangeable. Therefore, knowing This to be such, thou oughtest not to mourn.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the Self is unseen, beyond thinking, and never changes. Knowing this, Arjuna should not grieve."},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अथ चैनं नित्यजातं नित्यं वा मन्यसे मृतम् ।\nतथापि त्वं महाबाहो नैवं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥","iast":"atha cainaṃ nityajātaṃ nityaṃ vā manyase mṛtam |\ntathāpi tvaṃ mahābāho naivaṃ śocitumarhasi ||","read":"atha chainam nityajaatam nityam vaa manyase mritam |\ntathaapi tvam mahaabaaho naivam shochitumarhasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Or if thou thinkest of him as being constantly born and constantly dying, even then, O mighty-armed, thou shouldst not grieve.","en2":"But if thou shouldst take This to have constant birth and death, even in that case, O mighty-armed, thou oughtest not to mourn for This.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that even if Arjuna thinks of the one who lives in the body as always being born and always dying, he still should not grieve."},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्युर्ध्रुवं जन्म मृतस्य च ।\nतस्मादपरिहार्येऽर्थे न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥","iast":"jātasya hi dhruvo mṛtyurdhruvaṃ janma mṛtasya ca |\ntasmādaparihārye’rthe na tvaṃ śocitumarhasi ||","read":"jaatasya hi dhruvo mrityurdhruvam janma mritasya cha |\ntasmaadaparihaarye'rthe na tvam shochitumarhasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For certain is death for the born, and certain is birth for the dead; therefore over the inevitable thou shouldst not grieve.","en2":"Of that which is born, death is certain, of that which is dead, birth is certain. Over the unavoidable, therefore, thou oughtest not to grieve.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says death is certain for whatever is born, and birth is certain for whatever dies. So Arjuna should not grieve over what cannot be avoided."},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अव्यक्तादीनि भूतानि व्यक्तमध्यानि भारत ।\nअव्यक्तनिधनान्येव तत्र का परिदेवना ॥","iast":"avyaktādīni bhūtāni vyaktamadhyāni bhārata |\navyaktanidhanānyeva tatra kā paridevanā ||","read":"avyaktaadeeni bhootaani vyaktamadhyaani bhaarata |\navyaktanidhanaanyeva tatra kaa paridevanaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Beings are unmanifest in their origin, manifest in their midmost state, O Bhârata, unmanifest likewise are they in dissolution. What room then for lamentation?","en2":"All beings are unmanifested in their beginning, O Bhârata, manifested in their middle state and unmanifested again in their end. What is there then to grieve about?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says all beings are unseen at their beginning, seen in their middle, and unseen again at their end. So what is there to grieve about?"},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आश्चर्यवत्पश्यति कश्चिदेन ।\nमाश्चर्यवद्वदति तथैव चान्यः ।\nआश्चर्यवच्चैनमन्यः शृणोति ।\nश्रुत्वाप्येनं वेद न चैव कश्चित् ॥","iast":"āścaryavatpaśyati kaścidena |\nmāścaryavadvadati tathaiva cānyaḥ |\nāścaryavaccainamanyaḥ śṛṇoti |\nśrutvāpyenaṃ veda na caiva kaścit ||","read":"aashcharyavatpashyati kashchidena |\nmaashcharyavadvadati tathaiva chaanyah |\naashcharyavachchainamanyah shrinoti |\nshrutvaapyenam veda na chaiva kashchit ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As marvellous one regardeth him; as marvellous another speaketh thereof; as marvellous another heareth thereof; yet having heard none indeed understandeth.","en2":"Some look upon the Self as marvellous. Others speak of It as wonderful. Others again hear of It as a wonder. And still others, though hearing, do not understand It at all.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says some people see the Self as a wonder. Others speak of it as a wonder, and others hear of it as a wonder. Yet even after hearing of it, people do not understand it."},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"देही नित्यमवध्योऽयं देहे सर्वस्य भारत ।\nतस्मात्सर्वाणि भूतानि न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥","iast":"dehī nityamavadhyo’yaṃ dehe sarvasya bhārata |\ntasmātsarvāṇi bhūtāni na tvaṃ śocitumarhasi ||","read":"dehee nityamavadhyo'yam dehe sarvasya bhaarata |\ntasmaatsarvaani bhootaani na tvam shochitumarhasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This dweller in the body of everyone is ever invulnerable, O Bhârata; therefore thou shouldst not grieve for any creature.","en2":"This, the Indweller in the bodies of all, is ever indestructible, O descendant of Bharata. Wherefore thou oughtest not to mourn for any creature.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that the one who lives in every body can never be harmed. So he should not grieve for any living being."},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स्वधर्ममपि चावेक्ष्य न विकम्पितुमर्हसि ।\nधर्म्याद्धि युद्धाच्छ्रेयोऽन्यत्क्षत्रियस्य न विद्यते ॥","iast":"svadharmamapi cāvekṣya na vikampitumarhasi |\ndharmyāddhi yuddhācchreyo’nyatkṣatriyasya na vidyate ||","read":"svadharmamapi chaavekshya na vikampitumarhasi |\ndharmyaaddhi yuddhaachchhreyo'nyatkshatriyasya na vidyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Further, looking to thine own duty thou shouldst not tremble; for there is nothing more welcome to a Kshattriya than righteous war.","en2":"Looking at thine own Dharma, also, thou oughtest not to waver, for there is nothing higher for a Kshatriya than a righteous war.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says Arjuna should look at his own duty and not waver. For a warrior, nothing is better than a fight for what is right."},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदृच्छया चोपपन्नं स्वर्गद्वारमपावृतम् ।\nसुखिनः क्षत्रियाः पार्थ लभन्ते युद्धमीदृशम् ॥","iast":"yadṛcchayā copapannaṃ svargadvāramapāvṛtam |\nsukhinaḥ kṣatriyāḥ pārtha labhante yuddhamīdṛśam ||","read":"yadrichchhayaa chopapannam svargadvaaramapaavritam |\nsukhinah kshatriyaah paartha labhante yuddhameedrisham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Happy the Kshattriyas, O Pârtha, who obtain such a fight, offered unsought as an open door to heaven.","en2":"Fortunate certainly are the Kshatriyas, O son of Prithâ, who are called to fight in such a battle, that comes unsought as an open gate to heaven.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says warriors are lucky when a fair battle like this comes to them without their asking. It is like an open door to heaven."},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अथ चेत्त्वमिमं धर्म्यं संग्रामं न करिष्यसि ।\nततः स्वधर्मं कीर्तिं च हित्वा पापमवाप्स्यसि ॥","iast":"atha cettvamimaṃ dharmyaṃ saṃgrāmaṃ na kariṣyasi |\ntataḥ svadharmaṃ kīrtiṃ ca hitvā pāpamavāpsyasi ||","read":"atha chettvamimam dharmyam samgraamam na karishyasi |\ntatah svadharmam keertim cha hitvaa paapamavaapsyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But if thou wilt not carry on this righteous warfare, then casting away thine own duty and thine honour, thou wilt incur sin.","en2":"But if thou refusest to engage in this righteous warfare, then, forfeiting thine own Dharma and honour, thou shalt incur sin.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that if Arjuna refuses to fight in this fair war, he will throw away his duty and his honour, and he will bring sin on himself."},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अकीर्तिं चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम् ।\nसंभावितस्य चाकीर्तिर्मरणादतिरिच्यते ॥","iast":"akīrtiṃ cāpi bhūtāni kathayiṣyanti te’vyayām |\nsaṃbhāvitasya cākīrtirmaraṇādatiricyate ||","read":"akeertim chaapi bhootaani kathayishyanti te'vyayaam |\nsambhaavitasya chaakeertirmaranaadatirichyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Men will recount thy perpetual dishonour, and, to one highly esteemed, dishonour exceedeth death.","en2":"The world also will ever hold thee in reprobation. To the honoured, disrepute is surely worse than death.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that people will speak of his dishonour for ever. For someone who has been honoured, dishonour is worse than death."},{"v":35,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"भयाद्रणादुपरतं मंस्यन्ते त्वां महारथाः ।\nयेषां च त्वं बहुमतो भूत्वा यास्यसि लाघवम् ॥","iast":"bhayādraṇāduparataṃ maṃsyante tvāṃ mahārathāḥ |\nyeṣāṃ ca tvaṃ bahumato bhūtvā yāsyasi lāghavam ||","read":"bhayaadranaaduparatam mamsyante tvaam mahaarathaah |\nyeshaam cha tvam bahumato bhootvaa yaasyasi laaghavam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The great car-warriors will think thee fled from the battle from fear, and thou, that wast highly thought of by them, wilt be lightly held.","en2":"The great chariot-warriors will believe that thou hast withdrawn from the battle through fear. And thou wilt be lightly esteemed by them who have thought much of thee.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the great chariot warriors will think Arjuna ran from the battle out of fear. Those who once thought highly of him will think little of him."},{"v":36,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अवाच्यवादांश्च बहून् वदिष्यन्ति तवाहिताः ।\nनिन्दन्तस्तव सामर्थ्यं ततो दुःखतरं नु किम् ॥","iast":"avācyavādāṃśca bahūn vadiṣyanti tavāhitāḥ |\nnindantastava sāmarthyaṃ tato duḥkhataraṃ nu kim ||","read":"avaachyavaadaamshcha bahoon vadishyanti tavaahitaah |\nnindantastava saamarthyam tato duhkhataram nu kim ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Many unseemly words will be spoken by thine enemies, slandering thy strength; what more painful than that?","en2":"Thine enemies also, cavilling at thy great prowess, will say of thee things that are not to be uttered. What could be more intolerable than this?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says his enemies will say many unkind things and mock his strength. What could hurt more than that?"},{"v":37,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"हतो वा प्राप्स्यसि स्वर्गं जित्वा वा भोक्ष्यसे महीम् ।\nतस्मादुत्तिष्ठ कौन्तेय युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः ॥","iast":"hato vā prāpsyasi svargaṃ jitvā vā bhokṣyase mahīm |\ntasmāduttiṣṭha kaunteya yuddhāya kṛtaniścayaḥ ||","read":"hato vaa praapsyasi svargam jitvaa vaa bhokshyase maheem |\ntasmaaduttishtha kaunteya yuddhaaya kritanishchayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Slain, thou wilt obtain heaven; victorious, thou wilt enjoy the earth; therefore stand up, O son of Kuntî, resolute to fight.","en2":"Dying thou gainest heaven; conquering thou enjoyest the earth. Therefore, O son of Kunti, arise, resolved to fight.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that if he is killed, he will reach heaven. If he wins, he will enjoy the earth. So he should stand up, ready to fight."},{"v":38,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सुखदुःखे समे कृत्वा लाभालाभौ जयाजयौ ।\nततो युद्धाय युज्यस्व नैवं पापमवाप्स्यसि ॥","iast":"sukhaduḥkhe same kṛtvā lābhālābhau jayājayau |\ntato yuddhāya yujyasva naivaṃ pāpamavāpsyasi ||","read":"sukhaduhkhe same kritvaa laabhaalaabhau jayaajayau |\ntato yuddhaaya yujyasva naivam paapamavaapsyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Taking as equal pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat, gird thee for the battle; thus thou shalt not incur sin.","en2":"Having made pain and pleasure, gain and loss, conquest and defeat, the same, engage thou then in battle. So shalt thou incur no sin.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says to treat pleasure and pain, gain and loss, winning and losing as the same, and then go into battle. That way Arjuna will not bring sin on himself."},{"v":39,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एषा तेऽभिहिता साङ्ख्ये बुद्धिर्योगे त्विमां शृणु ।\nबुद्ध्या युक्तो यया पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यसि ॥","iast":"eṣā te’bhihitā sāṅkhye buddhiryoge tvimāṃ śṛṇu |\nbuddhyā yukto yayā pārtha karmabandhaṃ prahāsyasi ||","read":"eshaa te'bhihitaa saankhye buddhiryoge tvimaam shrinu |\nbuddhyaa yukto yayaa paartha karmabandham prahaasyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This teaching set forth to thee is in accordance with the Sâñkhya; hear it now according to the Yoga, imbued with which teaching, O Pârtha, thou shalt cast away the bonds of action.","en2":"The wisdom of Self-realisation has been declared unto thee. Hearken thou now to the wisdom of Yoga, endued with which, O son of Prithâ, thou shalt break through the bonds of Karma.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he has explained one kind of wisdom. Now Arjuna should hear another, and with it he will break free from the chains of his actions."},{"v":40,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नेहाभिक्रमनाशोऽस्ति प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते ।\nस्वल्पमप्यस्य धर्मस्य त्रायते महतो भयात् ॥","iast":"nehābhikramanāśo’sti pratyavāyo na vidyate |\nsvalpamapyasya dharmasya trāyate mahato bhayāt ||","read":"nehaabhikramanaasho'sti pratyavaayo na vidyate |\nsvalpamapyasya dharmasya traayate mahato bhayaat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"In this there is no loss of effort, nor is there transgression. Even a little of this knowledge protects from great fear.","en2":"In this, there is no waste of the unfinished attempt, nor is there production of contrary results. Even very little of this Dharma protects from the great terror.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that on this path no effort is wasted and nothing turns out wrong. Even a little of it protects a person from great fear."},{"v":41,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"व्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिरेकेह कुरुनन्दन ।\nबहुशाखा ह्यनन्ताश्च बुद्धयोऽव्यवसायिनाम् ॥","iast":"vyavasāyātmikā buddhirekeha kurunandana |\nbahuśākhā hyanantāśca buddhayo’vyavasāyinām ||","read":"vyavasaayaatmikaa buddhirekeha kurunandana |\nbahushaakhaa hyanantaashcha buddhayo'vyavasaayinaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The determinate Reason is but one-pointed, O joy of the Kurus; many-branched and endless are the thoughts of the irresolute.","en2":"In this, O scion of Kuru, there is but a single one-pointed determination. The purposes of the undecided are innumerable and many-branching.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a firm mind is fixed on one point. But the thoughts of people who cannot decide are endless and branch out in many directions."},{"v":42,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यामिमां पुष्पितां वाचं प्रवदन्त्यविपश्चितः ।\nवेदवादरताः पार्थ नान्यदस्तीति वादिनः ॥","iast":"yāmimāṃ puṣpitāṃ vācaṃ pravadantyavipaścitaḥ |\nvedavādaratāḥ pārtha nānyadastīti vādinaḥ ||","read":"yaamimaam pushpitaam vaacham pravadantyavipashchitah |\nvedavaadarataah paartha naanyadasteeti vaadinah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Flowery speech is uttered by the foolish, rejoicing in the letter of the Vedas, O Pârtha, saying: \"There is naught but this\";","en2":"O Pârtha, no set determination is formed in the minds of those that are deeply attached to pleasure and power, and whose discrimination is stolen away by the flowery words of the unwise, who are full of desires and look upon heaven as their highest goal and who, taking pleasure in the panegyric words of the Vedas, declare that there is nothing else. Their (flowery) words are exuberant with various specific, rites as the means to pleasure and power and are the causes of [paragraph continues] (new) births as the result of their works (performed with desire).","en2r":"2.42-44","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says unwise people speak flowery words. They delight in the words of the Vedas and say there is nothing else."},{"v":43,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कामात्मानः स्वर्गपरा जन्मकर्मफलप्रदाम् ।\nक्रियाविशेषबहुलां भोगैश्वर्यगतिं प्रति ॥","iast":"kāmātmānaḥ svargaparā janmakarmaphalapradām |\nkriyāviśeṣabahulāṃ bhogaiśvaryagatiṃ prati ||","read":"kaamaatmaanah svargaparaa janmakarmaphalapradaam |\nkriyaavisheshabahulaam bhogaishvaryagatim prati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"With desire for self, with heaven for goal, they offer birth as the fruit of action, and prescribe many and various ceremonies for the attainment of pleasure and lordship.","en2":"O Pârtha, no set determination is formed in the minds of those that are deeply attached to pleasure and power, and whose discrimination is stolen away by the flowery words of the unwise, who are full of desires and look upon heaven as their highest goal and who, taking pleasure in the panegyric words of the Vedas, declare that there is nothing else. Their (flowery) words are exuberant with various specific, rites as the means to pleasure and power and are the causes of [paragraph continues] (new) births as the result of their works (performed with desire).","en2r":"2.42-44","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says these people are full of desire and see heaven as their goal. They speak of many rituals for gaining pleasure and power, which lead to new births."},{"v":44,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"भोगैश्वर्यप्रसक्तानां तयापहृतचेतसाम् ।\nव्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिः समाधौ न विधीयते ॥","iast":"bhogaiśvaryaprasaktānāṃ tayāpahṛtacetasām |\nvyavasāyātmikā buddhiḥ samādhau na vidhīyate ||","read":"bhogaishvaryaprasaktaanaam tayaapahritachetasaam |\nvyavasaayaatmikaa buddhih samaadhau na vidheeyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For them who cling to pleasure and lordship, whose minds are captivated by such teaching, is not designed this determinate Reason, on contemplation steadily bent.","en2":"O Pârtha, no set determination is formed in the minds of those that are deeply attached to pleasure and power, and whose discrimination is stolen away by the flowery words of the unwise, who are full of desires and look upon heaven as their highest goal and who, taking pleasure in the panegyric words of the Vedas, declare that there is nothing else. Their (flowery) words are exuberant with various specific, rites as the means to pleasure and power and are the causes of [paragraph continues] (new) births as the result of their works (performed with desire).","en2r":"2.42-44","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says people who cling to pleasure and power, and whose minds are carried off by such words, cannot form a firm and steady mind."},{"v":45,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"त्रैगुण्यविषया वेदा निस्त्रैगुण्यो भवार्जुन ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो नित्यसत्त्वस्थो निर्योगक्षेम आत्मवान् ॥","iast":"traiguṇyaviṣayā vedā nistraiguṇyo bhavārjuna |\nnirdvandvo nityasattvastho niryogakṣema ātmavān ||","read":"traigunyavishayaa vedaa nistraigunyo bhavaarjuna |\nnirdvandvo nityasattvastho niryogakshema aatmavaan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Vedas deal with the three attributes; be thou above these three attributes, O Arjuna; beyond the pairs of opposites, ever steadfast in purity, careless of possessions, full of the Self.","en2":"The Vedas deal with the three Gunas. Be thou free, O Arjuna, from the triad of the Gunas, free from the pairs of opposites, ever-balanced, free from (the thought of) getting and keeping, and established in the Self.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that the Vedas deal with three qualities, and he should rise above them. He should be free of the pairs of opposites, always steady, not caring about getting and keeping things, and rooted in the Self."},{"v":46,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः संप्लुतोदके ।\nतावान्सर्वेषु वेदेषु ब्राह्मणस्य विजानतः ॥","iast":"yāvānartha udapāne sarvataḥ saṃplutodake |\ntāvānsarveṣu vedeṣu brāhmaṇasya vijānataḥ ||","read":"yaavaanartha udapaane sarvatah samplutodake |\ntaavaansarveshu vedeshu braahmanasya vijaanatah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All the Vedas are as useful to an enlightened Brâhmana as is a tank in a place covered all over with water.","en2":"To the Brâhmana who has known the Self, all the Vedas are of so much use as a reservoir is, when there is a flood everywhere.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that to someone who has truly known the Self, all the Vedas are as useful as a water tank is when there is a flood everywhere."},{"v":47,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।\nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥","iast":"karmaṇyevādhikāraste mā phaleṣu kadācana |\nmā karmaphalaheturbhūrmā te saṅgo’stvakarmaṇi ||","read":"karmanyevaadhikaaraste maa phaleshu kadaachana |\nmaa karmaphalaheturbhoormaa te sango'stvakarmani ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thy business is with the action only, never with its fruits; so let not the fruit of action be thy motive, nor be thou to inaction attached.","en2":"Thy right is to work only; but never to the fruits thereof. Be thou not the producer of the fruits of (thy) actions; neither let thy attachment be towards inaction.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that his part is the work itself, never its results. He should not work for the results, and he should not cling to doing nothing either."},{"v":48,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते ॥","iast":"yogasthaḥ kuru karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā dhanañjaya |\nsiddhyasiddhyoḥ samo bhūtvā samatvaṃ yoga ucyate ||","read":"yogasthah kuru karmaani sangam tyaktvaa dhananjaya |\nsiddhyasiddhyoh samo bhootvaa samatvam yoga uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Perform action, O Dhananjaya, dwelling in union with the divine, renouncing attachments and balanced evenly in success and failure: equilibrium is called yoga.","en2":"Being steadfast in Yoga, Dhananjaya, perform actions, abandoning attachment, remaining unconcerned as regards success and failure. This evenness. of mind (in regard to success and failure) is known as Yoga.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to do his work while letting go of attachment, and to stay the same whether he succeeds or fails. That evenness of mind is what Krishna is teaching."},{"v":49,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय ।\nबुद्धौ शरणमन्विच्छ कृपणाः फलहेतवः ॥","iast":"dūreṇa hyavaraṃ karma buddhiyogāddhanañjaya |\nbuddhau śaraṇamanviccha kṛpaṇāḥ phalahetavaḥ ||","read":"doorena hyavaram karma buddhiyogaaddhananjaya |\nbuddhau sharanamanvichchha kripanaah phalahetavah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Far lower than the Yoga of Discrimination is action, O Dhananjaya. Take thou refuge in the Pure Reason; pitiable are they who work for fruit.","en2":"Work (with desire) is verily far inferior to that performed with the mind undisturbed by thoughts of results. O [paragraph continues] Dhananjaya, seek refuge in this evenness of mind. Wretched are they who act for results.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says work done while wanting results is far lower than work done with a calm, even mind. Arjuna should hold to that even mind. Those who work for results are to be pitied."},{"v":50,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते ।\nतस्माद्योगाय युज्यस्व योगः कर्मसु कौशलम् ॥","iast":"buddhiyukto jahātīha ubhe sukṛtaduṣkṛte |\ntasmādyogāya yujyasva yogaḥ karmasu kauśalam ||","read":"buddhiyukto jahaateeha ubhe sukritadushkrite |\ntasmaadyogaaya yujyasva yogah karmasu kaushalam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"United to the Pure Reason one abandoneth here both good and evil deeds; therefore cleave thou to yoga; yoga is skill in action.","en2":"Endued with this evenness of mind, one frees oneself in this life, alike from vice and virtue. Devote thyself, therefore, to this Yoga. Yoga is the very dexterity of work.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that with this even mind, a person becomes free of both good and bad deeds, even in this life. So Arjuna should hold to it, because it is skill in action."},{"v":51,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मजं बुद्धियुक्ता हि फलं त्यक्त्वा मनीषिणः ।\nजन्मबन्धविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छन्त्यनामयम् ॥","iast":"karmajaṃ buddhiyuktā hi phalaṃ tyaktvā manīṣiṇaḥ |\njanmabandhavinirmuktāḥ padaṃ gacchantyanāmayam ||","read":"karmajam buddhiyuktaa hi phalam tyaktvaa maneeshinah |\njanmabandhavinirmuktaah padam gachchhantyanaamayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Sages, united to the Pure Reason, renounce the fruit which action yieldeth, and, liberated from the bonds of birth, they go to the blissful seat.","en2":"The wise, possessed of this evenness of mind, abandoning the fruits of their actions, freed for ever from the fetters of birth, go to that state which is beyond all evil.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says wise people with this even mind give up the results of their actions. Freed from the chains of birth, they go to a blessed state."},{"v":52,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा ते मोहकलिलं बुद्धिर्व्यतितरिष्यति ।\nतदा गन्तासि निर्वेदं श्रोतव्यस्य श्रुतस्य च ॥","iast":"yadā te mohakalilaṃ buddhirvyatitariṣyati |\ntadā gantāsi nirvedaṃ śrotavyasya śrutasya ca ||","read":"yadaa te mohakalilam buddhirvyatitarishyati |\ntadaa gantaasi nirvedam shrotavyasya shrutasya cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When thy mind shall escape from this tangle of delusion, then thou shalt rise to indifference as to what has been heard and shall be heard.","en2":"When thy intellect crosses beyond the taint of illusion, then shalt thou attain to indifference, regarding things heard and things yet to be heard.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that when his mind gets out of this tangle of confusion, he will no longer care about things he has heard or will yet hear."},{"v":53,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति निश्चला ।\nसमाधावचला बुद्धिस्तदा योगमवाप्स्यसि ॥","iast":"śrutivipratipannā te yadā sthāsyati niścalā |\nsamādhāvacalā buddhistadā yogamavāpsyasi ||","read":"shrutivipratipannaa te yadaa sthaasyati nishchalaa |\nsamaadhaavachalaa buddhistadaa yogamavaapsyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When thy mind, bewildered by the Scriptures, shall stand immovable, fixed in contemplation, then shalt thou attain unto yoga.","en2":"When thy intellect, tossed about by the conflict of opinions—has become immovable and firmly established in the Self, then thou shalt attain Self-realisation.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that his mind is now confused by many different words. When it becomes still, steady and fixed, he will reach the goal."},{"v":54,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"स्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा समाधिस्थस्य केशव ।\nस्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत किमासीत व्रजेत किम् ॥","iast":"sthitaprajñasya kā bhāṣā samādhisthasya keśava |\nsthitadhīḥ kiṃ prabhāṣeta kimāsīta vrajeta kim ||","read":"sthitaprajnasya kaa bhaashaa samaadhisthasya keshava |\nsthitadheeh kim prabhaasheta kimaaseeta vrajeta kim ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: What the mark, of him who is stable of mind, steadfast in contemplation, O Keshava? How doth the stable-minded talk, how doth he sit, how walk?","en2":"What, O Keshava, is the description of the man of steady wisdom, merged in Samâdhi? How (on the other hand) does the man of steady wisdom speak, how sit, how walk?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna what marks a person whose mind is steady and whose wisdom is firm. How does such a person speak, sit and walk?"},{"v":55,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"प्रजहाति यदा कामान् सर्वान् पार्थ मनोगतान् ।\nआत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते ॥","iast":"prajahāti yadā kāmān sarvān pārtha manogatān |\nātmanyevātmanā tuṣṭaḥ sthitaprajñastadocyate ||","read":"prajahaati yadaa kaamaan sarvaan paartha manogataan |\naatmanyevaatmanaa tushtah sthitaprajnastadochyate ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: When a man abandoneth, O Pârtha, all the desires of the heart, and is satisfied in the Self by the Self, then is he called stable in mind.","en2":"When a man completely casts away, O Pârtha, all the desires of the mind, satisfied in the Self alone by the Self, then is he said to be one of steady wisdom.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that when a person gives up all the desires of the mind and is content in the Self, by the Self, that person is called steady in wisdom."},{"v":56,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः ।\nवीतरागभयक्रोधः स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते ॥","iast":"duḥkheṣvanudvignamanāḥ sukheṣu vigataspṛhaḥ |\nvītarāgabhayakrodhaḥ sthitadhīrmunirucyate ||","read":"duhkheshvanudvignamanaah sukheshu vigatasprihah |\nveetaraagabhayakrodhah sthitadheermuniruchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He whose mind is free from anxiety amid pains, indifferent amid pleasures, loosed from passion, fear and anger, is called a sage of stable mind.","en2":"He whose mind is not shaken by adversity, who does not hanker after happiness, who has become free from affection, fear, and wrath, is indeed the Muni of steady wisdom.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a person whose mind is not shaken by pain, who does not chase after pleasure, and who is free from clinging, fear and anger, is a wise one with a steady mind."},{"v":57,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहस्तत्तत्प्राप्य शुभाशुभम् ।\nनाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","iast":"yaḥ sarvatrānabhisnehastattatprāpya śubhāśubham |\nnābhinandati na dveṣṭi tasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","read":"yah sarvatraanabhisnehastattatpraapya shubhaashubham |\nnaabhinandati na dveshti tasya prajnaa pratishthitaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who on every side is without attachments, whatever hap of fair and foul, who neither likes nor dislikes, of such a one the understanding is well poised.","en2":"He who is everywhere unattached, not pleased at receiving good, nor vexed at evil, his wisdom is fixed.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a person who clings to nothing, who is not thrilled by good things or upset by bad things, has wisdom that is steady."},{"v":58,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा संहरते चायं कूर्मोऽङ्गानीव सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","iast":"yadā saṃharate cāyaṃ kūrmo’ṅgānīva sarvaśaḥ |\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyastasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","read":"yadaa samharate chaayam koormo'ngaaneeva sarvashah |\nindriyaaneendriyaarthebhyastasya prajnaa pratishthitaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When, again, as a tortoise draws in on all sides its limbs, he withdraws his senses from the objects of sense, then is his understanding well poised.","en2":"When also, like the tortoise its limbs, he can completely withdraw the senses from their objects, then his wisdom becomes steady.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that like a tortoise pulling in its legs, a wise person can pull the senses back from the things around them. Then that person's wisdom is steady."},{"v":59,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विषया विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः ।\nरसवर्जं रसोऽप्यस्य परं दृष्ट्वा निवर्तते ॥","iast":"viṣayā vinivartante nirāhārasya dehinaḥ |\nrasavarjaṃ raso’pyasya paraṃ dṛṣṭvā nivartate ||","read":"vishayaa vinivartante niraahaarasya dehinah |\nrasavarjam raso'pyasya param drishtvaa nivartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The objects of sense, but not the relish for them, turn away from an abstemious dweller in the body; and even relish turneth away from him after the Supreme is seen.","en2":"Objects fall away from the abstinent man, leaving the longing behind. But his longing also ceases, who sees the Supreme.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that when a person holds back from things, the things fall away, but the longing for them stays. Even the longing goes once that person has seen the Supreme."},{"v":60,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यततो ह्यपि कौन्तेय पुरुषस्य विपश्चितः ।\nइन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः ॥","iast":"yatato hyapi kaunteya puruṣasya vipaścitaḥ |\nindriyāṇi pramāthīni haranti prasabhaṃ manaḥ ||","read":"yatato hyapi kaunteya purushasya vipashchitah |\nindriyaani pramaatheeni haranti prasabham manah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"O son of Kuntî, the excited senses of even a wise man, though he be striving, impetuously carry away his mind.","en2":"The turbulent senses, O son of Kunti, do violently snatch away the mind of even a wise man, striving after perfection.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that the restless senses can pull away the mind of even a wise person who is trying hard."},{"v":61,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तानि सर्वाणि संयम्य युक्त आसीत मत्परः ।\nवशे हि यस्येन्द्रियाणि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","iast":"tāni sarvāṇi saṃyamya yukta āsīta matparaḥ |\nvaśe hi yasyendriyāṇi tasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","read":"taani sarvaani samyamya yukta aaseeta matparah |\nvashe hi yasyendriyaani tasya prajnaa pratishthitaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having restrained them all, he should sit harmonised, I his supreme goal; for, whose senses are mastered, of him the understanding is well poised.","en2":"The steadfast, having controlled them all, sits focussed on Me as the Supreme. His wisdom is steady, whose senses are under control.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a person should control all the senses and sit steady, with Krishna as the highest goal. Someone whose senses are under control has steady wisdom."},{"v":62,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ध्यायतो विषयान्पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते ।\nसङ्गात् संजायते कामः कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते ॥","iast":"dhyāyato viṣayānpuṃsaḥ saṅgasteṣūpajāyate |\nsaṅgāt saṃjāyate kāmaḥ kāmātkrodho’bhijāyate ||","read":"dhyaayato vishayaanpumsah sangasteshoopajaayate |\nsangaat samjaayate kaamah kaamaatkrodho'bhijaayate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Man, musing on the objects of sense, conceiveth an attachment to these; from attachment ariseth desire; from desire anger cometh forth;","en2":"Thinking of objects, attachment to them is formed in a man. From attachment longing, and from longing anger grows.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that when a person keeps thinking about things, attachment to them grows. From attachment comes longing, and from longing comes anger."},{"v":63,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"क्रोधाद्भवति संमोहः संमोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः ।\nस्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति ॥","iast":"krodhādbhavati saṃmohaḥ saṃmohātsmṛtivibhramaḥ |\nsmṛtibhraṃśād buddhināśo buddhināśātpraṇaśyati ||","read":"krodhaadbhavati sammohah sammohaatsmritivibhramah |\nsmritibhramshaad buddhinaasho buddhinaashaatpranashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"From anger proceedeth delusion; from delusion confused memory; from confused memory the destruction of Reason; from destruction of Reason he perishes.","en2":"From anger comes delusion, and from delusion loss of memory. From loss of memory comes the ruin of discrimination, and from the ruin of discrimination he perishes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says anger leads to confusion, and confusion to a muddled memory. A muddled memory destroys good judgement, and when good judgement is gone, the person perishes."},{"v":64,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रागद्वेषवियुक्तैस्तु विषयानिन्द्रियैश्चरन् ।\nआत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"rāgadveṣaviyuktaistu viṣayānindriyaiścaran |\nātmavaśyairvidheyātmā prasādamadhigacchati ||","read":"raagadveshaviyuktaistu vishayaanindriyaishcharan |\naatmavashyairvidheyaatmaa prasaadamadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But the disciplined self, moving among sense-objects with senses free from attraction and repulsion, mastered by the Self, goeth to peace.","en2":"But the self-controlled man, moving among objects with senses under restraint, and free from attraction and aversion, attains to tranquillity.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a self-controlled person moves among things with the senses held in check, free from liking and disliking, and reaches peace."},{"v":65,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रसादे सर्वदुःखानां हानिरस्योपजायते ।\nप्रसन्नचेतसो ह्याशु बुद्धिः पर्यवतिष्ठते ॥","iast":"prasāde sarvaduḥkhānāṃ hānirasyopajāyate |\nprasannacetaso hyāśu buddhiḥ paryavatiṣṭhate ||","read":"prasaade sarvaduhkhaanaam haanirasyopajaayate |\nprasannachetaso hyaashu buddhih paryavatishthate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"In that Peace the extinction of all pains ariseth for him, for of him whose heart is peaceful the Reason soon attaineth equilibrium.","en2":"In tranquillity, all sorrow is destroyed. For the intellect of him who is tranquil-minded, is soon established in firmness.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that in that peace, all sorrow ends. The mind of a peaceful person soon becomes firm and steady."},{"v":66,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना ।\nन चाभावयतः शान्तिरशान्तस्य कुतः सुखम् ॥","iast":"nāsti buddhirayuktasya na cāyuktasya bhāvanā |\nna cābhāvayataḥ śāntiraśāntasya kutaḥ sukham ||","read":"naasti buddhirayuktasya na chaayuktasya bhaavanaa |\nna chaabhaavayatah shaantirashaantasya kutah sukham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"There is no Pure Reason for the non-harmonised, nor for the non-harmonised is there concentration; for him without concentration there is no peace, and for the unpeaceful how can there be happiness?","en2":"No knowledge (of the Self) has the unsteady. Nor has he meditation. To the unmeditative there is no peace. And how can one without peace have happiness?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says an unsteady person has no true understanding and cannot focus. Without focus there is no peace, and without peace, how can anyone be happy?"},{"v":67,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इन्द्रियाणां हि चरतां यन्मनोऽनुविधीयते ।\nतदस्य हरति प्रज्ञां वायुर्नावमिवाम्भसि ॥","iast":"indriyāṇāṃ hi caratāṃ yanmano’nuvidhīyate |\ntadasya harati prajñāṃ vāyurnāvamivāmbhasi ||","read":"indriyaanaam hi charataam yanmano'nuvidheeyate |\ntadasya harati prajnaam vaayurnaavamivaambhasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Such of the roving senses as the mind yieldeth to, that hurries away the understanding, just as the gale hurries away a ship upon the waters.","en2":"For, the mind which follows in the wake of the wandering senses, carries away his discrimination, as a wind (carries away from its course) a boat on the waters.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that when the mind follows the wandering senses, it carries away a person's understanding, just as the wind carries a boat away on the water."},{"v":68,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तस्माद्यस्य महाबाहो निगृहीतानि सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥","iast":"tasmādyasya mahābāho nigṛhītāni sarvaśaḥ |\nindriyāṇīndriyārthebhyastasya prajñā pratiṣṭhitā ||","read":"tasmaadyasya mahaabaaho nigriheetaani sarvashah |\nindriyaaneendriyaarthebhyastasya prajnaa pratishthitaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore, O mighty-armed, whose senses are all completely restrained from the objects of sense, of him the understanding is well poised.","en2":"Therefore, O mighty-armed, his knowledge is steady, whose senses are completely restrained from their objects.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"So, Krishna tells Arjuna, a person whose senses are fully held back from the things around them has steady wisdom."},{"v":69,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"या निशा सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी ।\nयस्यां जाग्रति भूतानि सा निशा पश्यतो मुनेः ॥","iast":"yā niśā sarvabhūtānāṃ tasyāṃ jāgarti saṃyamī |\nyasyāṃ jāgrati bhūtāni sā niśā paśyato muneḥ ||","read":"yaa nishaa sarvabhootaanaam tasyaam jaagarti samyamee |\nyasyaam jaagrati bhootaani saa nishaa pashyato muneh ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which is the night of all beings, for the disciplined man is the time of waking; when other beings are waking, then is it night for the sage who seeth.","en2":"That which is night to all beings, in that the self-controlled man wakes. That in which all beings wake, is night to the Self-seeing Muni.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that what is night for all beings is a time of waking for the self-controlled person. And when all other beings are awake, it is night for the wise one who sees."},{"v":70,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं ।\nसमुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत् ।\nतद्वत्कामा यं प्रविशन्ति सर्वे ।\nस शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी ॥","iast":"āpūryamāṇamacalapratiṣṭhaṃ |\nsamudramāpaḥ praviśanti yadvat |\ntadvatkāmā yaṃ praviśanti sarve |\nsa śāntimāpnoti na kāmakāmī ||","read":"aapooryamaanamachalapratishtham |\nsamudramaapah pravishanti yadvat |\ntadvatkaamaa yam pravishanti sarve |\nsa shaantimaapnoti na kaamakaamee ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He attaineth Peace, into whom all desires flow as rivers flow into the ocean, which is filled with water, but remaineth unmoved—not he who desireth desires.","en2":"As into the ocean,—brimful, and still,—flow the waters, even so the Muni into whom enter all desires, he, and not the desirer of desires, attains to peace.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the ocean stays full and still, though rivers keep flowing into it. A person who stays still like that while desires flow in finds peace, not one who chases desires."},{"v":71,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विहाय कामान्यः सर्वान्पुमांश्चरति निःस्पृहः ।\nनिर्ममो निरहंकारः स शांतिमधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"vihāya kāmānyaḥ sarvānpumāṃścarati niḥspṛhaḥ |\nnirmamo nirahaṃkāraḥ sa śāṃtimadhigacchati ||","read":"vihaaya kaamaanyah sarvaanpumaamshcharati nihsprihah |\nnirmamo nirahamkaarah sa shaamtimadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whoso forsaketh all desires and goeth onwards free from yearnings, selfless and without egoism—he goeth to Peace.","en2":"That man who lives devoid of longing, abandoning all desires, without the sense of 'I' and 'mine,' he attains to peace.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says a person who gives up all desires and lives free of longing and selfishness reaches peace."},{"v":72,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति ।\nस्थित्वाऽस्यामन्तकालेऽपि ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति ॥","iast":"eṣā brāhmī sthitiḥ pārtha naināṃ prāpya vimuhyati |\nsthitvā’syāmantakāle’pi brahmanirvāṇamṛcchati ||","read":"eshaa braahmee sthitih paartha nainaam praapya vimuhyati |\nsthitvaa'syaamantakaale'pi brahmanirvaanamrichchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This is the Eternal state, O son of Prithâ. Having attained thereto, none is bewildered. Who, even at the death-hour, is established therein, he goeth to the Nirvâna of the Eternal.","en2":"This is to have one's being in Brahman, O son of Prithâ. None, attaining to this, becomes deluded. Being established therein, even at the end of life, a man attains to oneness with Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that this is the eternal state. Whoever reaches it is never confused. Whoever stays in it, even at the hour of death, reaches the Eternal."}];
